# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_resolve_rust_super_item.py" "RUST-SUPER-ITEM GATE: PASS" "rust super item resolve" "Rust super::/self:: trailing ITEM-name recall: when the relative tail is a single identifier that is not a submodule, fall back to the PARENT MODULE FILE (climb/mod.rs or climb.rs) with a unique-match precision guard and self-edge drop; submodule resolution keeps precedence; no parent file stays unresolved" "Rust relative-import recall: use super::ReadBuf resolves async_read.rs to io/mod.rs (the parent module file that re-exports/defines the item) instead of dropping the edge after the nonexistent ReadBuf.rs submodule probe misses; measured 36 dropped intra-crate edges on tokio; recall-safe and unique-match only; does not touch crate::/Go/CSharp/PHP branches" 14
